WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.362
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.662 --> 00:00:09.141
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.441 --> 00:00:14.160
Unit four: Plural Nouns. Today you will talk about more than one thing.

4
00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:16.961
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:21.040
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:21.883 --> 00:00:22.617
Cat.

7
00:00:23.617 --> 00:00:25.814
Cat means a small furry pet animal.

8
00:00:26.417 --> 00:00:27.604
I have one cat.

9
00:00:28.217 --> 00:00:30.660
Your turn. Say: Cat.

10
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:34.269
Cat.

11
00:00:35.017 --> 00:00:35.890
Cats.

12
00:00:36.883 --> 00:00:38.813
Cats means more than one cat.

13
00:00:39.417 --> 00:00:40.743
She has two cats.

14
00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:44.072
Your turn. Say: Cats.

15
00:00:46.933 --> 00:00:48.004
Cats.

16
00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:49.635
Box.

17
00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:53.102
Box means a container with four sides.

18
00:00:53.717 --> 00:00:55.217
The box is on the table.

19
00:00:55.817 --> 00:00:58.504
Your turn. Say: Box.

20
00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:02.275
Box.

21
00:01:03.017 --> 00:01:03.925
Boxes.

22
00:01:04.917 --> 00:01:07.021
Boxes means more than one box.

23
00:01:07.617 --> 00:01:09.384
Three boxes are in the room.

24
00:01:09.983 --> 00:01:12.612
Your turn. Say: Boxes.

25
00:01:15.467 --> 00:01:16.584
Boxes.

26
00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:18.165
Child.

27
00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:21.231
Child means a young boy or girl.

28
00:01:21.817 --> 00:01:23.271
The child is happy.

29
00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:26.199
Your turn. Say: Child.

30
00:01:29.033 --> 00:01:29.860
Child.

31
00:01:30.617 --> 00:01:31.455
Children.

32
00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:34.519
Children means more than one child.

33
00:01:35.117 --> 00:01:36.849
The children play outside.

34
00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:39.394
Your turn. Say: Children.

35
00:01:42.233 --> 00:01:43.060
Children.

36
00:01:43.817 --> 00:01:44.725
Regular.

37
00:01:45.717 --> 00:01:48.041
Regular means following the normal rule.

38
00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:50.499
Most plurals are regular.

39
00:01:51.083 --> 00:01:53.724
Your turn. Say: Regular.

40
00:01:56.567 --> 00:01:57.626
Regular.

41
00:01:58.383 --> 00:01:59.396
Irregular.

42
00:02:00.383 --> 00:02:03.555
Irregular means not following the normal rule.

43
00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:05.987
Child is an irregular noun.

44
00:02:06.583 --> 00:02:09.131
Your turn. Say: Irregular.

45
00:02:11.967 --> 00:02:13.037
Irregular.

46
00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:17.902
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:21.272
Visal, how do we say more than one cat?

48
00:02:22.383 --> 00:02:30.367
We say cats. Most nouns are regular. We add s: one cat, two cats; one book, two books.

49
00:02:31.483 --> 00:02:32.717
What about box?

50
00:02:33.817 --> 00:02:44.991
After s, x, ch and sh, we add es: one box, two boxes; one watch, two watches. It is easier to say.

51
00:02:46.083 --> 00:02:47.944
Are there any special plurals?

52
00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:59.503
Yes. Some are irregular. One child, two children. One man, two men. One foot, two feet. Sheep and fish stay the same.

53
00:03:00.667 --> 00:03:01.865
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:02.717 --> 00:03:07.178
Grammar focus: Plural nouns: -s and -es and irregular.

55
00:03:07.478 --> 00:03:08.711
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:09.417 --> 00:03:11.056
cat + s cats

57
00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:13.787
box + es boxes

58
00:03:14.683 --> 00:03:16.427
child irregular children

59
00:03:17.367 --> 00:03:25.084
Add s to most nouns. Add es after s, x, ch and sh. Some nouns are irregular: child becomes children.

60
00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:29.036
Be careful! Don't say: I have two childs.

61
00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:32.849
Say: I have two children.

62
00:03:33.149 --> 00:03:35.090
Child is irregular: children.

63
00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:38.680
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:39.467 --> 00:03:40.561
One and Many.

65
00:03:40.861 --> 00:03:43.417
I have one cat, but my friend has three cats.

66
00:03:44.433 --> 00:03:47.443
There is one box on the table and two boxes under it.

67
00:03:48.433 --> 00:03:51.362
The child is small, and the children are in the garden.

68
00:03:52.367 --> 00:03:55.074
Most nouns are regular, so we add s.

69
00:03:56.067 --> 00:03:59.076
A few nouns are irregular, so we must remember them.

70
00:04:00.167 --> 00:04:04.226
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:05.083 --> 00:04:06.839
One cat, two blank.

72
00:04:07.139 --> 00:04:10.375
A, cat. B, cats. C, cates.

73
00:04:13.933 --> 00:04:15.794
The answer is B: cats.

74
00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:18.683
One box, three blank.

75
00:04:18.983 --> 00:04:22.926
A, boxs. B, boxes. C, boxies.

76
00:04:26.467 --> 00:04:28.304
The answer is B: boxes.

77
00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:31.136
One child, many blank.

78
00:04:31.436 --> 00:04:35.240
A, childs. B, childes. C, children.

79
00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:40.474
The answer is C: children.

80
00:04:41.617 --> 00:04:43.256
Which noun is irregular?

81
00:04:43.556 --> 00:04:46.641
A, dog. B, man. C, pen.

82
00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:51.770
The answer is B: man.

83
00:04:52.917 --> 00:04:56.193
According to the reading, how many boxes are under the table?

84
00:04:56.493 --> 00:04:59.404
A, one. B, two. C, three.

85
00:05:02.967 --> 00:05:04.653
The answer is B: two.

86
00:05:05.867 --> 00:05:09.587
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:12.415
What is the plural form of 'child'?

88
00:05:21.217 --> 00:05:22.659
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:22.959 --> 00:05:36.356
The plural form of child is children. It is an irregular plural, so we do not add s. We say one child and two children. I must remember this word because it does not follow the regular rule.

90
00:05:36.656 --> 00:05:38.284
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:39.183 --> 00:05:45.470
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and plural nouns: -s and -es and irregular.

92
00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:49.351
Today's value is attention. Look carefully and listen well.

93
00:05:49.651 --> 00:05:52.199
See you in Unit five. Goodbye!

94
00:05:52.499 --> 00:05:56.440
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

